From 71f66cc44c345bfac70123638abf7cc19eef6b28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:20:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign: restore the site's own frosted-glass card system
 and polish the landing gate

- Remove transparent-cards.css (and its <link>). It force-flattened
  every .glass-card/.glass-header/.glass-nav/.glass-chip, the hero
  banner, chat bubbles, status badges, IMBL/verdict panels, satellite
  and bulletin cards, and terminal panes to background:transparent,
  which was silently defeating the whole frosted-glass design system
  already built into styles.css (--glass-bg/--glass-border/--glass-
  shadow, the diagonal sheen, per-state tints). Deleting it restores
  that intended glass effect everywhere, in both day and night theme,
  with zero markup/ID/class changes -- every element already carried
  the right classes, they just wasn't allowed to paint.
- Give .text-gradient a real gradient (cyan -> teal -> steel-blue)
  instead of a flat color, and drop data-varweight-force="true" from
  the two gradient headings so variable-weight-headings.js keeps
  treating them as gradient text (its own documented behavior) instead
  of splitting them into per-letter spans, which would have broken the
  gradient into illegible per-letter fragments.
- Polish the landing gate: an eyebrow label, a soft pulsing ring behind
  the ORCA mark, staggered reveal-in motion (reusing the existing
  .reveal/.revealed system already driven by app.js), and a 'tap
  anywhere to enter' cue -- purely additive markup/CSS, no IDs touched,
  orcaEnterDashboard()/orcaBackToLanding() untouched.

No changes to app.js, backend/*, ais_gateway.py, route_planner.py,
config.js, manifest.json, or any data/asset file -- functionality
(AIS live feed, Open-Meteo, Mappls map, day/night toggle, i18n, DAG
visualizer, NavIC, SOS) is untouched, this is visual-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M6baXCyXms78ADfWemjjUo
